WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.833 --> 00:00:30.083


2
00:00:30.083 --> 00:00:32.166
<b>Here, Krishna explains</b>

3
00:00:32.166 --> 00:00:37.458
<b>that those who remain trapped in </b>
<b>material pleasures and attachments</b>

4
00:00:37.458 --> 00:00:40.916
<b>maintain a disturbed state of mind,</b>

5
00:00:40.916 --> 00:00:44.916
<b>and can never achieve true focus.</b>

6
00:00:49.625 --> 00:00:52.541
<b>When a person becomes engrossed </b>
<b>in desires for a comfortable life,</b>

7
00:00:52.541 --> 00:00:57.875
<b>sensual pleasures, wealth, or fame,</b>

8
00:00:57.875 --> 00:01:02.375
<b>their mind becomes confused and wanders.</b>

9
00:01:02.375 --> 00:01:03.416
<b>In such a state,</b>

10
00:01:03.416 --> 00:01:09.750
<b>this person, completely absorbed in </b>
<b>materialism,overlooks their spirituality</b>

11
00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:14.375
<b>and soon completely forgets </b>
<b>this spiritual essence.</b>

12
00:01:14.375 --> 00:01:21.208
<b>As a result, this person abandons the path </b>
<b>of selfless action (Nishkam Karma Yoga).</b>

13
00:01:21.208 --> 00:01:24.833
<b>Both their interest in understanding </b>
<b>the body-soul relationship</b>

14
00:01:24.833 --> 00:01:30.000
<b>and their yearning for</b>
<b> spiritual wisdom fade away.</b>

15
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:36.750
<b>They become entirely absorbed in sensual </b>
<b>pleasures, materialism, and indulgence.</b>

16
00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:38.500
<b>If this continues,</b>

17
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:46.875
<b>the person soon loses all willpower to achieve </b>
<b>anything great or purposeful in their life.</b>

18
00:01:46.875 --> 00:01:51.666
<b>And when the negative consequences of </b>
<b>being absorbed in materialism surface,</b>

19
00:01:51.666 --> 00:01:54.458
<b>only then do they feel remorse.</b>

20
00:01:59.166 --> 00:02:01.500
<b>Often it happens</b>

21
00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:06.625
<b>that we make firm resolutions</b>
<b> to change our lives,</b>

22
00:02:06.625 --> 00:02:10.625
<b>announce them, make plans,</b>

23
00:02:10.625 --> 00:02:15.166
<b>and at the planning stage it all feels wonderful,</b>

24
00:02:15.166 --> 00:02:16.375
<b>but</b>

25
00:02:16.375 --> 00:02:23.583
<b>after taking just a few steps, that firmness</b>
<b>of resolve seems to vanish,</b>

26
00:02:23.583 --> 00:02:26.708
<b>plans remain incomplete,</b>

27
00:02:26.708 --> 00:02:34.625
<b>and within days we find ourselves back in the</b>
<b>same situation we were in before.</b>

28
00:02:34.625 --> 00:02:39.875
<b>Instead of plans, all that remain are excuses</b>

29
00:02:39.875 --> 00:02:45.333
<b>for why we couldn't follow through.</b>

30
00:02:45.333 --> 00:02:49.541
<b>This happens with our work too.</b>

31
00:02:49.541 --> 00:02:55.125
<b>We feel this job isn't meant for us, we'll change,</b>

32
00:02:55.125 --> 00:02:59.458
<b>we'll do something more meaningful.</b>

33
00:02:59.458 --> 00:03:00.750
<b>But</b>

34
00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:07.541
<b>within a short time, we're trapped </b>
<b>in the same old cycle again.</b>

35
00:03:07.541 --> 00:03:10.291
<b>Why does this happen?</b>

36
00:03:10.291 --> 00:03:17.416
<b>Why can't we stick to our resolutions and plans?</b>

37
00:03:17.416 --> 00:03:20.708
<b>There are two reasons:</b>

38
00:03:20.708 --> 00:03:23.375
<b>The desire for sensual pleasures.</b>

39
00:03:23.375 --> 00:03:25.125
<b>And Second</b>

40
00:03:25.125 --> 00:03:30.416
<b>the pursuit of wealth to obtain these pleasures</b>

41
00:03:30.416 --> 00:03:35.166
<b>These two factors distract us from our goals,</b>

42
00:03:35.166 --> 00:03:40.375
<b>defeating our plans for life transformation.</b>

43
00:03:40.375 --> 00:03:42.250
<b>For example</b>

44
00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:45.750
<b>you make a firm resolution </b>
<b>to improve your health,</b>

45
00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:48.500
<b>decide to eat healthy food,</b>

46
00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:54.833
<b>but then sensual pleasure tempts you, and for </b>
<b>the taste of the tongue, we're again</b>

47
00:03:54.833 --> 00:04:01.833
<b>attracted to food that doesn't serve our purpose.</b>

48
00:04:01.833 --> 00:04:04.500
<b>Now you don't want to give up</b>
<b>the pleasure of taste,</b>

49
00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:07.708
<b>but you also want to be healthy,</b>

50
00:04:07.708 --> 00:04:11.875
<b>so you're drawn to expensive gyms, </b>

51
00:04:11.875 --> 00:04:16.000
<b>you spend money on them.</b>

52
00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.250
<b>And after some time,</b>

53
00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:20.583
<b>you abandon them too.</b>

54
00:04:20.583 --> 00:04:23.458
<b>Life returns to the same pattern</b>

55
00:04:23.458 --> 00:04:29.291
<b>wanting taste, wanting pleasure, </b>
<b>wanting an expensive lifestyle,</b>

56
00:04:29.291 --> 00:04:32.208
<b>and for all this,</b>

57
00:04:32.208 --> 00:04:35.458
<b>wanting money.</b>

58
00:04:35.458 --> 00:04:36.875
<b>Here,</b>

59
00:04:36.875 --> 00:04:38.708
<b>taste isn't wrong,</b>

60
00:04:38.708 --> 00:04:40.166
<b>pleasure isn't bad,</b>

61
00:04:40.166 --> 00:04:42.041
<b>money isn't evil,</b>

62
00:04:42.041 --> 00:04:42.916
<b>but</b>

63
00:04:42.916 --> 00:04:47.541
<b>becoming their slave, depending on them?</b>

64
00:04:47.541 --> 00:04:49.583
<b>That's certainly wrong.</b>

65
00:04:49.583 --> 00:04:54.875
<b>Breaking your firm resolution</b>
<b>to transform your life every time,</b>

66
00:04:54.875 --> 00:05:00.958
<b>forgetting promises made</b>
<b>to yourself, that's wrong.</b>

67
00:05:00.958 --> 00:05:05.041
<b>Does this happen with you?</b>

68
00:05:05.041 --> 00:05:08.041
<b>Ask yourself,</b>

69
00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:14.875
<b>aren't you getting trapped in this</b>
<b>cycle of sensual cravings? </b>

70
00:05:14.875 --> 00:05:19.166
<b>Spirituality will help you in self-control.</b>

71
00:05:19.166 --> 00:05:22.750
<b>It will be useful in achieving life's goals.</b>

72
00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:27.166
<b>This Gita will show you the right path.</b>

73
00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:37.750
<b>Loyalty to each other and </b>
<b>commitment to the relationship</b>

74
00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:42.916
<b>these two elements form the foundation </b>
<b>of a successful married life.</b>

75
00:05:42.916 --> 00:05:46.875
<b>If either breaks,</b>

76
00:05:46.875 --> 00:05:51.708
<b>the marriage can fall apart.</b>

77
00:05:51.708 --> 00:05:52.666
<b>But</b>

78
00:05:52.666 --> 00:05:57.250
<b>many people fear such steady commitment.</b>

79
00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:01.208
<b>What if they have to commit to one partner?</b>

80
00:06:01.208 --> 00:06:03.833
<b>What about life's other experiences?</b>

81
00:06:03.833 --> 00:06:06.750
<b>What about enjoyment?</b>

82
00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:12.041
<b>For this reason, they run away </b>
<b>from married life itself.</b>

83
00:06:12.041 --> 00:06:13.291
<b>Similarly,</b>

84
00:06:13.291 --> 00:06:18.125
<b>there are many who enter married life</b>

85
00:06:18.125 --> 00:06:25.416
<b>but don't want to control </b>
<b>their comfort, their desires.</b>

86
00:06:25.416 --> 00:06:27.041
<b>Gradually,</b>

87
00:06:27.041 --> 00:06:30.375
<b>that relationship weakens.</b>

88
00:06:30.375 --> 00:06:31.333
<b>Sometimes</b>

89
00:06:31.333 --> 00:06:35.250
<b>the outer structure of </b>
<b>that relationship still shines,</b>

90
00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:40.000
<b>but inside everything has become hollow.</b>

91
00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:46.833
<b>And here we're not just talking </b>
<b>about bodily desires.</b>

92
00:06:46.833 --> 00:06:53.333
<b>Two people in a relationship</b>
<b>may need to make many compromises</b>

93
00:06:53.333 --> 00:06:56.458
<b>now you might like something, </b>

94
00:06:56.458 --> 00:07:00.416
<b>but your partner doesn't,</b>

95
00:07:00.416 --> 00:07:05.250
<b>so you might need to exercise</b>
<b>control in such matters too.</b>

96
00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:06.875
<b>Consider this</b>

97
00:07:06.875 --> 00:07:15.500
<b>you've taken a vow to spend life together, </b>
<b>but small desires break that vow.</b>

98
00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:21.458
<b>Far more joyful than </b>
<b>these desires are mutual love,</b>

99
00:07:21.458 --> 00:07:31.500
<b>loyalty to each other, a commitment that </b>
<b>will last a lifetime, in happiness and sorrow.</b>

100
00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:33.958
<b>How beautiful is this thought</b>

101
00:07:33.958 --> 00:07:38.416
<b>having a partner present in </b>
<b>every up and down of life.</b>

102
00:07:38.416 --> 00:07:40.083
<b>Momentary desires, </b>

103
00:07:40.083 --> 00:07:41.041
<b>or</b>

104
00:07:41.041 --> 00:07:44.833
<b>a lifetime of fulfilling relationship.</b>

105
00:07:44.833 --> 00:07:48.833
<b>You know the right choice.</b>

106
00:07:48.833 --> 00:07:50.625
<b>Think about it.</b>

107
00:07:55.291 --> 00:07:58.375
<b>Today working in one organization,</b>

108
00:07:58.375 --> 00:07:59.916
<b>tomorrow in another,</b>

109
00:07:59.916 --> 00:08:03.583
<b>then after some time in a third.</b>

110
00:08:03.583 --> 00:08:07.750
<b>In professional life, this changing is common.</b>

111
00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:09.875
<b>Happens.</b>

112
00:08:09.875 --> 00:08:11.041
<b>But</b>

113
00:08:11.041 --> 00:08:14.458
<b>what's the reason behind it?</b>

114
00:08:14.458 --> 00:08:16.583
<b>There are several reasons</b>

115
00:08:16.583 --> 00:08:18.208
<b>higher salary,</b>

116
00:08:18.208 --> 00:08:19.958
<b>better benefits,</b>

117
00:08:19.958 --> 00:08:23.125
<b>or a bigger position.</b>

118
00:08:23.125 --> 00:08:26.208
<b>Is any of this wrong?</b>

119
00:08:26.208 --> 00:08:29.458
<b>No, absolutely not.</b>

120
00:08:29.458 --> 00:08:33.875
<b>These are all natural, life's necessities.</b>

121
00:08:33.875 --> 00:08:37.583
<b>So then what's wrong?</b>

122
00:08:37.583 --> 00:08:41.750
<b>Understand here the difference </b>
<b>between necessity and craving.</b>

123
00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:50.708
<b>What's wrong is making the craving for salary, </b>
<b>benefits, and position your life's purpose.</b>

124
00:08:50.708 --> 00:08:53.875
<b>There's no end to any of these</b>

125
00:08:53.875 --> 00:08:55.125
<b>not to salary,</b>

126
00:08:55.125 --> 00:08:56.416
<b>not to benefits,</b>

127
00:08:56.416 --> 00:08:58.333
<b>not to position.</b>

128
00:08:58.333 --> 00:09:02.708
<b>If you start considering </b>
<b>these as your supreme purpose,</b>

129
00:09:02.708 --> 00:09:07.166
<b>you'll lose your way in life.</b>

130
00:09:07.166 --> 00:09:11.541
<b>You'll tire yourself changing</b>
<b>from one path to another,</b>

131
00:09:11.541 --> 00:09:21.333
<b>and unfortunately, you won't see your </b>
<b>destination anywhere in sight.</b>

132
00:09:21.333 --> 00:09:23.458
<b>So what should be done now?</b>

133
00:09:23.458 --> 00:09:25.500
<b>Know these two things:</b>

134
00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:26.750
<b>First</b>

135
00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:27.666
<b>Salary,</b>

136
00:09:27.666 --> 00:09:29.625
<b>position, benefits...</b>

137
00:09:29.625 --> 00:09:32.625
<b>can be milestones,</b>

138
00:09:32.625 --> 00:09:35.458
<b>but never life goals.</b>

139
00:09:35.458 --> 00:09:37.041
<b>Second</b>

140
00:09:37.041 --> 00:09:41.166
<b>Search for your life's inner purpose.</b>

141
00:09:41.166 --> 00:09:44.791
<b>This purpose will bring joy to your mind,</b>

142
00:09:44.791 --> 00:09:46.208
<b>and because</b>

143
00:09:46.208 --> 00:09:49.375
<b>you're now on the right path,</b>

144
00:09:49.375 --> 00:09:53.458
<b>you won't wander or tire.</b>

145
00:09:53.458 --> 00:09:54.500
<b>But</b>

146
00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:59.750
<b>how to find life's purpose?</b>

147
00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:00.833
<b>For that,</b>

148
00:10:00.833 --> 00:10:06.750
<b>I will guide you through this Gita.</b>

